A||||6||87GT||88GT Tires||||1||
Z||000000||87GT||02-05-2001||03:11 PM||||I am buying a 88GT that needs new tires so I want to put some on order before it gets here, but I need to know what the factory tire specs are for a 88GT.  I know there different, but dont know the size.  Thanks.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000001||Formula88||02-05-2001||03:32 PM||||Congrats on the '88!  The tire sizes are 205/60-15 front and 215/60-15 rear.  Also note that in '88 the front and rear wheels are different sizes with different offset.  When I picked up my 88 Formula, it had the right size tires, but the rear wheels on the front and front wheels on the rear.  Talk about screwing up the handling!  Fixing that was the first thing I did to the car.  The rear wheels are wider than the front, but the easiest way to tell with tires mounted is to check the offset.  On the rear wheels, the silver rim sticks out from the cross lace section by about an inch.  On the front wheels, the cross lace section is almost flush with the silver part of the rim.<P>------------------<BR>We all come into this world the same way; naked, screaming, and covered in blood.  If you're lucky, it doesn't have to end there.||||reg||10
Z||000002||Black88GT||02-05-2001||03:55 PM||||Also the wheels are labeled FRONT and REAR so its hard to screw it up, but people still do it.  On both of the '88s I have owned, they both had the 215's on the front, changing them makes big difference.<P>For whats it worth, I got BFG Comp T/A's, and they are great.  <P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/cartmanico.gif">             <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/kennyico.gif">           <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/stanico.gif">         <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/kyleico.gif">             <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/chefico.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||87GT||02-05-2001||04:33 PM||||Well those are the same sizes as my 87GT tires.  I thought the 88s had a universal size because of the suspension change. I guess not.. Thanks Guys!  ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Formula88||02-05-2001||06:11 PM||||Where does it say Front and Rear on the rims?  Just got mine recently, so I haven't covered EVERY inch of it, yet....  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR>We all come into this world the same way; naked, screaming, and covered in blood.  If you're lucky, it doesn't have to end there.||||reg||5
Z||000005||PJ||02-05-2001||08:54 PM||||I've been using 225/60's in the rear for a while now (Yoko AVS'). Kept the 205/60's up front. Still, the rears will wear about twice as fast as the fronts but not as fast as the 215's. The 225's fill up the wheelwell better and the car looks more aggressive with the rear a little higher than the front.||||reg||1
Z||000006||KissMySSFiero||02-05-2001||10:03 PM||||ive got 225 read and 205 front as well.  the rim says 15x6x37mm, front only, made in USA, 10080821,  and western wheel corp and a few others that are hard to read.  a while ago i hit a curb racin someone in a parking lot.  wont do that again.  but i blew one tire and made a bubble in the other.  so when i had them replaced the put the 225 tire on the front rim and 205 on the front and had the rims in the wrong spot.  bad thing is i told the service writer to have the guy make sure he got it right.  seeing how i have never had anyone do any work on my car up the that point i was paranoid something like this was going to happen.  go figure.  <P>------------------<BR>JOEJOE Aol:KissMySSFiero <P>88FORMULA<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:KissMySSFiero@netzero.net">KissMySSFiero@netzero.net</A>   <P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FORUMSIG1.jpg">       <BR>"There's a fine line between love and beer"<BR><A HREF="http://expage.com/kissmyssfiero" TARGET=_blank>KissMySSFiero.mywebsite.hehe</A>||||reg||1
